{
  "info": {
    "name": "RobinKeyz — User",
    "description": "Registration, profile and the admin user list.\n\n### Setup\nSelect the **RobinKeyz — Local** environment, then send **Login** from the *RobinKeyz — Auth* collection once. That saves `accessToken` to the environment and every request here picks it up.\n\n### Validation\nThe global ValidationPipe uses `whitelist` and `forbidNonWhitelisted`, so any field that is not in the DTO returns **400**.\n\n### Who can call what\n| Route | Allowed |\n|---|---|\n| `POST /users/register` | anyone |\n| `GET /users/me` | any logged-in user |\n| `GET /users/all-user` | admin |\n| `GET /users/:id` | admin, user |\n| `DELETE /users/:id` | admin |",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{accessToken}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "User",
      "description": "Registration, profile and the admin user list.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Register",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// A fresh email each run, so this never hits the 409 conflict.",
                  "pm.environment.set('newUserEmail', 'sayed' + Date.now() + '@example.com');"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 201', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('User is created unverified', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(body.data.user).to.have.property('id');",
                  "  pm.expect(body.data.user.isEmailVerified).to.eql(false);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Verification token is returned', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(body.data).to.have.property('token');",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Password is not exposed', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(body.data.user).to.not.have.property('password');",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "// Needed by Verify Email OTP and Resend Email OTP.",
                  "if (body.data && body.data.token) {",
                  "  pm.environment.set('verifyEmailToken', body.data.token);",
                  "}",
                  "if (body.data && body.data.user) {",
                  "  pm.environment.set('userId', body.data.user.id);",
                  "  console.log('userId', body.data.user.id, '| verifyEmailToken saved');",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Abu Sayed\",\n  \"email\": \"{{newUserEmail}}\",\n  \"phone\": \"01712345678\",\n  \"password\": \"{{newUserPassword}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{apiUrl}}/users/register",
              "host": [
                "{{apiUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "users",
                "register"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Creates a user with `isEmailVerified: false`, emails a 6 digit OTP and returns a verification token.\n\nA pre-request script generates a new email each run. **Saves `verifyEmailToken` and `userId` to the environment automatically.**\n\n| Field | Rule |\n|---|---|\n| `name` | not empty |\n| `email` | valid email |\n| `phone` | any string |\n| `password` | at least 6 characters |\n\n**Expected:** 201.\n\nThe account cannot log in until **Verify Email OTP** succeeds."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Register — Again while Unverified (201)",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Signed Up Again\",\n  \"email\": \"{{newUserEmail}}\",\n  \"phone\": \"01799999999\",\n  \"password\": \"{{newUserPassword}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{apiUrl}}/users/register",
              "host": [
                "{{apiUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "users",
                "register"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Send **Register** first, then this one — it reuses the same email.\n\nBecause that account exists but is **not verified yet**, this is not treated as an error. The name, phone and password are refreshed, a new OTP is emailed, and a new token comes back.\n\n**Expected:** 201 — not 409.\n\nOnce the email *is* verified, the same request returns **409 — `User with this email already exists`**. Worth sending again after Verify Email OTP to see the difference."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 201, not 409', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Details were updated', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(body.data.user.name).to.eql('Signed Up Again');",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "// A fresh OTP was issued, so keep the newest token.",
                  "if (body.data && body.data.token) {",
                  "  pm.environment.set('verifyEmailToken', body.data.token);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Verify Email OTP",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Email is now verified', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().data.isEmailVerified).to.eql(true);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{verifyEmailToken}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"otp\": \"{{otp}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{apiUrl}}/users/verify-email-otp",
              "host": [
                "{{apiUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "users",
                "verify-email-otp"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Sends `verifyEmailToken`, not `accessToken`.\n\n**Put the code from your email into the `otp` environment variable first**, or type the digits straight into the body.\n\nOn success the OTP row is deleted, so the same code cannot be reused.\n\n**Expected:** 200 with `isEmailVerified: true`. The account can log in from now on.\n\n| Case | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Wrong code | 400 — `Wrong OTP` |\n| Older than 10 minutes | 400 — `OTP has expired` |\n| Already used | 404 — `OTP not found!` |\n| Already verified | 400 — `Email is already verified.` |"
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Resend Email OTP",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (body.data && body.data.token) {",
                  "  pm.environment.set('verifyEmailToken', body.data.token);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{verifyEmailToken}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{apiUrl}}/users/resend-email-otp",
              "host": [
                "{{apiUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "users",
                "resend-email-otp"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Did not get the email, or the code expired? This issues a new OTP and emails it again. Needs `verifyEmailToken`.\n\nThe previous code stops working. **Refreshes `verifyEmailToken` automatically.**\n\n**Expected:** 200. Already verified: 400 — `Email is already verified.`"
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Register — Invalid Email (400)",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Bad Email\",\n  \"email\": \"not-an-email\",\n  \"phone\": \"01712345678\",\n  \"password\": \"secret123\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{apiUrl}}/users/register",
              "host": [
                "{{apiUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "users",
                "register"
              ]
            },
            "description": "**Expected:** 400 — `email must be an email`."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Register — Short Password (400)",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Short Pass\",\n  \"email\": \"shortpass@example.com\",\n  \"phone\": \"01712345678\",\n  \"password\": \"123\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{apiUrl}}/users/register",
              "host": [
                "{{apiUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "users",
                "register"
              ]
            },
            "description": "**Expected:** 400 — `password must be longer than or equal to 6 characters`."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Register — Unknown Field (400)",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Extra Field\",\n  \"email\": \"extra@example.com\",\n  \"phone\": \"01712345678\",\n  \"password\": \"secret123\",\n  \"role\": \"admin\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{apiUrl}}/users/register",
              "host": [
                "{{apiUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "users",
                "register"
              ]
            },
            "description": "`role` is not in the DTO. Because `forbidNonWhitelisted` is on, the whole request is rejected instead of the field being dropped — so nobody can make themselves an admin at signup.\n\n**Expected:** 400 — `property role should not exist`."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Get My Profile",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Password is not exposed', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().data).to.not.have.property('password');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{apiUrl}}/users/me",
              "host": [
                "{{apiUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "users",
                "me"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The logged-in user's own profile, read fresh from the database.\n\n`GET /auth/me` returns the same shape but straight from the guard, without a second query.\n\n**Expected:** 200. Without a token: 401."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Get All Users (admin)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('data is an array', () => pm.expect(body.data).to.be.an('array'));",
                  "pm.test('pagination is present', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(body.pagination).to.have.property('totalItem');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{apiUrl}}/users/all-user?page=1&limit=10",
              "host": [
                "{{apiUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "users",
                "all-user"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "page",
                  "value": "1"
                },
                {
                  "key": "limit",
                  "value": "10"
                },
                {
                  "key": "searchTerm",
                  "value": "sayed",
                  "disabled": true,
                  "description": "Matches name, email or phone. Several words are ANDed."
                },
                {
                  "key": "role",
                  "value": "admin",
                  "disabled": true,
                  "description": "Any column name works as a filter: role, isDeleted, isEmailVerified"
                },
                {
                  "key": "isDeleted",
                  "value": "false",
                  "disabled": true,
                  "description": "Strings are cast, so true/false and numbers work"
                },
                {
                  "key": "sort",
                  "value": "-createdAt",
                  "disabled": true,
                  "description": "Comma separated. A leading - means descending."
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Admin only. Backed by the QueryBuilder, so search, filter, sort and pagination all work together.\n\nThe greyed-out params are examples — tick them in the **Params** tab to try them.\n\nResponse carries a `pagination` block:\n```json\n{ \"totalPage\": 3, \"currentPage\": 1, \"prevPage\": 1, \"nextPage\": 2, \"limit\": 2, \"totalItem\": 6 }\n```\n\n**Expected:** 200. As a non-admin: 403 — `You are not authorized.`"
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Get All Users — search + sort",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{apiUrl}}/users/all-user?searchTerm=sayed&sort=email&limit=5",
              "host": [
                "{{apiUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "users",
                "all-user"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "searchTerm",
                  "value": "sayed"
                },
                {
                  "key": "sort",
                  "value": "email"
                },
                {
                  "key": "limit",
                  "value": "5"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Searches name, email and phone, sorts by email ascending, five per page.\n\nTry `sort=-email` for descending, or `searchTerm=abu sayed` — each word must match something."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Get Single User",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{apiUrl}}/users/{{userId}}",
              "host": [
                "{{apiUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "users",
                "{{userId}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Uses the `userId` saved by **Register**, so send that first or set the variable yourself.\n\nOpen to admin and user.\n\n**Expected:** 200. Unknown or soft-deleted id: 404 — `User not found`."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Delete User (admin)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('success is true', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().success).to.eql(true);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{apiUrl}}/users/{{userId}}",
              "host": [
                "{{apiUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "users",
                "{{userId}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Soft delete — sets `isDeleted: true`, the row stays in the database.\n\nAfterwards that account cannot log in, and any token it already holds stops working, because both login and AuthGuard check `isDeleted`.\n\n**Expected:** 200.\n\n| Case | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Not an admin | 403 — `You are not authorized.` |\n| Target is an admin | 403 — `Cannot delete a admin account.` |\n| Sent twice | 400 — `User is already deleted.` |\n| Unknown id | 404 — `User not found.` |"
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
